  One refinement to something I said earlier. I told you I'd make the task model its own separate project. Having
  thought about the data model, I'd rather make it [1mone spec with two phases[0m — Phase 1 tasks (usable on its own), Phase 2
  reminders. Splitting the spec would mean designing the task record twice, once blind to what reminders need from it,
  and the task model here is small enough that the separation buys nothing. Same build order, one document.

  I'm also assuming [1mvanilla JS, no framework or build step[0m, to match a repo that is currently one static HTML file. Say
  if you'd rather I pull in a framework.

  [1mThe approaches[0m

  The fork is whether a notification is a [3mthing you store[0m or a [3mstate you compute[0m. That decision is expensive to reverse,
  because it determines whether there's a second persisted entity to keep in sync with tasks.

